      "Relevant principles:",
      "- Autonomy: respect informed refusal\n- Beneficence: recommend potentially helpful care\n- Nonmaleficence: explain foreseeable risk and avoid coercion\n- Veracity: provide accurate information\n- Fidelity: remain reliable and avoid punitive withdrawal",
      "The counselor should not equate disagreement with incapacity. The next step is usually to assess understanding and risk, explore the client's reasoning, discuss alternatives, document informed refusal, and continue appropriate care unless another legal or safety issue changes the analysis.",
