      "A professional code can:",
      "- Express the profession's core values\n- Define responsibilities shared by members or certificants\n- Guide ethical decision-making\n- Educate counselors and the public\n- Protect clients and the integrity of the profession\n- Establish standards for ethics complaints\n- Support professional identity\n- Help interpret emerging issues",
      "A code does not eliminate the need for judgment. The 2014 ACA Code specifically expects a carefully considered process and recognizes that no single decision-making model works best in every case.",
      "## Aspirational and enforceable content",
      "### Aspirational content",
      "Aspirational language describes values and ideals toward which professionals strive, such as social justice, human development, diversity, and integrity.",
      "### Enforceable standards",
      "Standards describe professional responsibilities and can support complaints or discipline within the adopting organization's authority.",
      "The distinction does not make aspirational content unimportant. Values and principles help interpret standards and guide decisions in new situations.",
      "## Current adopted ACA Code structure",
      "As of August 18, 2026, ACA identifies the 2014 Code as current. It contains sections addressing:",
