      "One event can trigger more than one process, but the processes are not interchangeable.",
      "## Code knowledge and interpretation",
      "Ethical competence requires more than remembering a section number. The counselor should:",
      "1. Confirm the current adopted version.\n2. Read the complete standard and its surrounding section.\n3. Determine whether the counselor is subject to that code.\n4. Identify relevant laws, regulations, and policies.\n5. Consider principles, culture, and client welfare.\n6. Apply a credible decision-making process.",
      "## Code as floor, guide, and accountability structure",
      "Ethical codes are often described as minimum standards, but this phrase should not be misunderstood. Counselors should not aim merely to avoid punishment. Good practice also considers:",
